          "text": "Item: leave it empty unless the tool is a family tool (different parts from different positions); a position with no item makes whatever item is running. Blocked: out of service for now; it still counts toward the standard rate, so the parts it isn't making show as a performance loss. Retired: out of service for good; it leaves the standard rate. Positions can't change while the tool is mounted: block a cavity from the mount panel, and retire it here once the tool is off the machine."
